<title>UK: DTB expects over half of one-month Euromark trade.</title>
<headline>DTB expects over half of one-month Euromark trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Terminboerse (DTB) board member Joerg Franke said on Thursday the German exchange expected to gain more than 50 percent of the trading volume in new one-month Euromark futures due to be launched this month.</p>
<p>The DTB is launching its one-month Euromark on November 12 while rival the London International Financial Futures and Options Exchange (LIFFE) will introduce its one-month future on November 21.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect to have more than 50 percent of the trading volume in the one-month Euromark future,&quot; Franke said in a speech prepared for delivery at a news conference here.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
</text>
